---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import { SITE } from "../../lib/site";
import { localizePath , pick } from "../../i18n/utils";

const lang = (Astro.currentLocale ?? "en") as "en" | "zh";

const slug = "icloud-sync";

const C = pick({
  en: {
    heading: "iCloud sync and Keychain",
    intro:
      "Your server list follows you between iPhone, iPad, and Mac through iCloud, while passwords and SSH keys stay in the Apple Keychain. Here is exactly what syncs and what does not.",
    meta: "Documentation",
    title: "iCloud sync and Keychain — VVTerm",
    description:
      "VVTerm syncs server metadata through iCloud while passwords and SSH keys stay in the Apple Keychain, syncing only through iCloud Keychain when you enable it.",
    schemaDescription:
      "How VVTerm syncs server metadata through iCloud while keeping passwords and SSH keys in the Apple Keychain, how deduplication works, and what does not sync.",
    bodyHtml: `
  <p>
    VVTerm keeps your setup consistent across devices by splitting your data into two parts: the
    server definitions that describe how to connect, and the secrets used to sign in. They are handled
    differently on purpose, so your list can travel freely while your credentials stay protected.
  </p>

  <h2>What syncs through iCloud</h2>
  <p>
    Server <strong>metadata</strong> syncs through iCloud using CloudKit. That includes the details you
    enter when <a href="/docs/adding-a-server">adding a server</a> — its name, host, port, username,
    and environment — along with your workspaces and how everything is organized. Add a server on your
    Mac and it appears on your iPhone and iPad; rename a workspace on one device and the change follows
    to the others.
  </p>

  <h2>What stays in the Keychain</h2>
  <p>
    Your secrets — <strong>passwords, private SSH keys, and passphrases</strong> — are stored in the <strong>Apple Keychain</strong>, not in the synced metadata. They are deliberately kept out of
    CloudKit, so the part of your data that moves through iCloud never contains a credential.
  </p>
  <p>
    Credentials move between your devices only when <strong>iCloud Keychain</strong> is enabled in your
    iOS or macOS settings. With it on, a saved password or key becomes available on your other devices
    through Apple's secure Keychain sync. With it off, credentials stay on the device where you entered
    them, and you add them again on each device you use.
  </p>

  <h2>What does not sync</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Credentials are never carried by CloudKit.</strong> Passwords and SSH keys are excluded from the synced server metadata entirely.</li>
    <li>If iCloud Keychain is off, your secrets do not leave the device, even though the server list still syncs.</li>
    <li>Active terminal sessions and connection tabs are local to a device and are not synced.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Deduplication</h2>
  <p>
    Each server and workspace carries a stable identifier. When VVTerm merges changes coming from
    iCloud, it matches records <strong>by ID</strong>, so the same server that exists on two devices is
    reconciled into a single entry rather than duplicated. This keeps your list clean even when you
    make edits on more than one device.
  </p>

  <h2>Working without iCloud</h2>
  <p>
    If iCloud is unavailable or turned off, VVTerm falls back to local storage so the app keeps working
    on that device. Your servers are saved locally and remain usable; they simply will not propagate to
    your other devices until iCloud sync is available again.
  </p>

  <h2>Next steps</h2>
  <p>
    To control how secrets are stored per server, see <a href="/docs/authentication-and-keys">Authentication and SSH keys</a>. To organize the servers
    that sync, see <a href="/docs/workspaces-and-tabs">Workspaces, environments, and tabs</a>.
  </p>
`,
  },
  zh: {
    heading: "iCloud 同步与 Keychain",
    intro:
      "你的服务器列表通过 iCloud 在 iPhone、iPad 和 Mac 之间跟随你，而密码和 SSH 密钥则保留在 Apple Keychain 中。这里准确说明哪些会同步、哪些不会。",
    meta: "文档",
    title: "iCloud 同步与 Keychain — VVTerm",
    description:
      "VVTerm 通过 iCloud 同步服务器元数据，而密码和 SSH 密钥保留在 Apple Keychain 中，仅在你启用 iCloud Keychain 时才同步。",
    schemaDescription:
      "VVTerm 如何通过 iCloud 同步服务器元数据，同时把密码和 SSH 密钥保留在 Apple Keychain 中、去重如何工作，以及哪些不会同步。",
    bodyHtml: `
  <p>
    VVTerm 通过把你的数据分成两部分来让设置在设备间保持一致：描述如何连接的服务器定义，以及用于登录的密钥。它们被有意区别对待，因此你的列表可以自由流转，而密钥始终受保护。
  </p>

  <h2>哪些通过 iCloud 同步</h2>
  <p>
    服务器<strong>元数据</strong>通过 iCloud 使用 CloudKit 同步。这包括你在<a href="/zh/docs/adding-a-server">添加服务器</a>时输入的细节 —— 名称、主机、端口、用户名和环境 —— 以及你的工作区和整体的组织方式。在 Mac 上添加一台服务器，它会出现在你的 iPhone 和 iPad 上；在一台设备上重命名一个工作区，更改会跟随到其他设备。
  </p>

  <h2>哪些保留在 Keychain 中</h2>
  <p>
    你的密钥 —— <strong>密码、SSH 私钥和口令</strong> —— 保存在 <strong>Apple Keychain</strong> 中，而非同步的元数据里。它们被有意排除在 CloudKit 之外，因此通过 iCloud 流转的那部分数据永远不包含密钥。
  </p>
  <p>
    只有当你的 iOS 或 macOS 设置中启用了 <strong>iCloud Keychain</strong> 时，密钥才会在设备间流转。开启后，已保存的密码或密钥会通过 Apple 安全的 Keychain 同步在你的其他设备上可用。关闭时，密钥留在你输入它的设备上，你需要在每台使用的设备上再次添加。
  </p>

  <h2>哪些不会同步</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>密钥永远不会由 CloudKit 携带。</strong>密码和 SSH 密钥被完全排除在同步的服务器元数据之外。</li>
    <li>如果 iCloud Keychain 关闭，即使服务器列表仍在同步，你的密钥也不会离开设备。</li>
    <li>活动的终端会话和连接标签页属于单台设备本地，不会被同步。</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>去重</h2>
  <p>
    每台服务器和工作区都带有一个稳定的标识符。当 VVTerm 合并来自 iCloud 的更改时，它<strong>按 ID</strong> 匹配记录，因此在两台设备上存在的同一台服务器会被合并成单个条目而非重复。即使你在多台设备上做了编辑，这也能让你的列表保持整洁。
  </p>

  <h2>在没有 iCloud 时工作</h2>
  <p>
    如果 iCloud 不可用或被关闭，VVTerm 会回退到本地存储，让应用在该设备上继续工作。你的服务器会保存在本地并保持可用；它们只是在 iCloud 同步再次可用前不会传播到你的其他设备。
  </p>

  <h2>后续步骤</h2>
  <p>
    要控制每台服务器如何存储密钥，参见<a href="/zh/docs/authentication-and-keys">认证与 SSH 密钥</a>。要整理同步的服务器，参见<a href="/zh/docs/workspaces-and-tabs">工作区、环境与标签页</a>。
  </p>
`,
  },
}, lang);

const articleSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "TechArticle",
  name: C.heading,
  description: C.schemaDescription,
  url: `${SITE.siteUrl}${localizePath(`/docs/${slug}`, lang)}`,
};
---

<DocsLayout
  kind="docs"
  activeSlug={slug}
  heading={C.heading}
  intro={C.intro}
  meta={C.meta}
  title={C.title}
  description={C.description}
  canonicalPath={`/docs/${slug}`}
  structuredData={[articleSchema]}
>
  <Fragment set:html={C.bodyHtml} />
</DocsLayout>
